    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "But you're saying it \"becomes a compelling moral imperative.\" That sounds like you're saying the choice has already been made if the math works out. If a democracy sits back and watches a genocide or a massive crackdown happen because they wanted to \"respect sovereignty,\" aren't they basically just being complicit? Why is sovereignty more \"real\" than the actual lives of the people living there?",
