      "content": "To frame it as complicity, one adopts a strong rights-based ethic where inaction in the face of known mass death is itself a moral failure. This perspective argues that sovereignty is not an absolute shield when a state actively violates fundamental human rights on a massive scale. Therefore, the intrinsic value of preserving human life often overrides the procedural value of respecting a nation's borders when genocide is imminent.",
      "source": "target",
